## 5. Resource Load (capacity view)

Swimlanes = assignees; overlapping bars stack and an over-allocation strip flags
when someone is double-booked. Turns the Gantt into a staffing/capacity read.

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│ Team load                              [ Lane: Assignee ▾ ]   [ Week ▾ ]      │
├──────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                  │  Jun        Jul        Aug        Sep       ┊ now          │
│ ● Alice    ▓▓▓▓  │  ▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓                                   ┊   load 1.0   │
│            load  │      ▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓                             ┊              │
│            ⚠ over│  ◀══ overlap Jun 24–Jul 2 ══▶                ┊             │
│ ● Bob      ▓▓    │           ▓▓▓▓▓▓                            ┊   load 0.6   │
│            load  │                     ▓▓▓▓▓                   ┊              │
│ ● Carol    ░     │                          ▓▓▓               ┊   load 0.3   │
│ ● Unassigned     │  ▓▓▓   ▓▓     ▓▓▓▓                          ┊   3 items    │
└──────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
   ▓ allocated   ⚠ over-allocated (overlapping bars)   load = Σ active / capacity
```

- **Data:** `groupBy` = user field; detect overlapping spans per lane.
- **Config:** `capacityPerLane` (default 1 concurrent); `⚠` strip on overlap; load badge.
- **Best for:** capacity planning, spotting double-booked owners across the timeline.

